The following test fixtures contain code components (public keys and example
HTTP signature fields) extracted from IETF documents:

* rfc9421-b24.json, rfc9421-b26.json, rfc9421-rsa-pss-public.txt:
  RFC 9421, "HTTP Message Signatures", February 2024, by Annabelle Backman,
  Justin Richer and Manu Sporny. Sections B.1.2, B.1.4, B.2.4 and B.2.6.
  https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9421.html
  Copyright (c) 2024 IETF Trust and the persons identified as authors of the
  code. All rights reserved.

* webbotauth-vectors.json:
  draft-ietf-webbotauth-httpsig-protocol-00, "HTTP Message Signatures for
  automated traffic", September 2026, by Thibault Meunier and Sandor Major.
  Sections E.1.1, E.1.2, E.2.1 and E.2.2. This is a version-pinned Internet
  Draft (work in progress), not a final standard.
  https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-webbotauth-httpsig-protocol-00.html
  Copyright (c) 2026 IETF Trust and the persons identified as authors of the
  code. All rights reserved.

The Ed25519 public key and canonicalization example reproduced in
../Unit/WebBotAuthTest.php originate from RFC 9421 as well. No private key
from either document is included in this repository. Fixtures are adapted
into JSON and include local test metadata; signature bytes are unchanged.

